 1094 and were beaten; a 30,000-strong army besieged Peña Cadiella in late 1096; Mazdali besieged Valencia in early spring 1102 and the Almoravids occupied it in April-May…","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Taifa_of_Valencia"},{"name":"Aragonese conquest of Valencia","from":1236,"to":1238,"outcome":"Aragon took Puig in 1236, besieged Valencia from 23 April 1238, and the city surrendered on 29 September 1238.","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Taifa_of_Valencia"}],"certainty":[{"from":1010,"to":1238,"level":"soft","note":"No treaty or survey line is given for the taifa's frontiers in any page opened; the extent of its district around Valencia is approximate throughout."}],"sources":[{"url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Taifa_of_Valencia","title":"Taifa of Valencia"},{"url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Taifa_of_Almería","title":"Taifa of Almería"},{"url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Taifa_of_Murcia","title":"Taifa of Murcia"},{"url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Muhammad_ibn_Sa%27d_ibn_Mardanish","title":"Muhammad ibn Sa'd ibn Mardanish"},{"url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kingdom_of_Valencia","title":"Kingdom of Valencia"}]}